  "issue_title": "[refactor] Split `tools/dispatch.rs` into per-tool modules behind a `ToolEntry` registry",
  "issue_body": "### What problem does this solve?\n\n`crates/genie-core/src/tools/dispatch.rs` is **3 328 lines** and is simultaneously doing five unrelated jobs:\n\n1. **Schema registry** \u2014 `tool_defs()` (lines 390\u2013561) embeds every tool's JSON schema as inline `serde_json::json!` literals scattered across ~170 lines of push/extend calls.\n2. **Dispatch table** \u2014 `execute_with_context` (lines 567\u2013640) routes every call through a single `match call.name.as_str()` arm.\n3. **Tool implementations** \u2014 `exec_memory_recall`, `exec_memory_status`, `exec_memory_forget`, `exec_memory_store`, `exec_home_control_inner`, `exec_play_media` all live as `impl ToolDispatcher` methods despite having zero coupling to the dispatcher's own fields.\n4. **Private utility** \u2014 argument parsers, rate limiter (`ActuationRateLimiter`), audit logger (`ToolAuditLogger`), and policy helpers are file-level free functions mixed with business logic.\n5. **Builder** \u2014 seven `with_*` methods that construct required state piece-by-piece.\n\nThe immediate cost is that adding a new tool requires touching `dispatch.rs` in **three separate places** (schema in `tool_defs`, arm in the match, implementation as a new `impl` method). The existing per-tool files (`calc.rs`, `system.rs`, `weather.rs`, `home.rs`) are unreachable from outside `dispatch.rs` without going through the dispatcher \u2014 there is no shared interface, so callers cannot compose tools independently in evaluation harness or tests.\n\n### Proposed feature\n\nIntroduce a `ToolEntry` trait that each compiled-in tool implements, then replace `dispatch.rs` with a thin registry + middleware layer:\n\n```rust\npub trait ToolEntry: Send + Sync {\n    fn name(&self) -> &str;\n    fn schema(&self) -> ToolDef;\n    fn enabled(&self) -> bool { true }\n    fn execute<'a>(\n        &'a self,\n        args: &'a serde_json::Value,\n        ctx: ToolExecutionContext,\n    ) -> std::pin::Pin<Box<dyn std::future::Future<Output = anyhow::Result<String>> + Send + 'a>>;\n}\n```\n\nThree new files replace the monolith:\n\n- **`tools/registry.rs`** \u2014 `ToolRegistry` holds a `Vec<Box<dyn ToolEntry>>`, drives `tool_defs()` and `dispatch()` without a central match arm.\n- **`tools/dispatcher.rs`** \u2014 `ToolDispatcher` wraps `ToolRegistry` and keeps the middleware choke-point: origin policy gate, rate limiter, confirmation gate, audit logging.\n- **`tools/config.rs`** \u2014 `ToolDispatcherConfig` struct replaces the seven `with_*` builder methods.\n\nPer-tool logic moves into `tools/builtin/` \u2014 one file per tool. Adding a new tool becomes: create one file, implement `ToolEntry`, register in `ToolRegistry::build()`.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n**Keep `dispatch.rs`, add section dividers.** Already tried (the file has region comments). Doesn't help IDEs, diff tools, or CI coverage attribution. The match arm still requires touching the same 3 000-line file for every tool change.\n\n**`enum Tool { HomeControl, WebSearch, ... }` instead of trait objects.** Avoids dynamic dispatch but still centralises every tool's schema and execute arm in one file \u2014 same problem as today.\n\n### Which milestone is this aimed at?\n\nM2 \u2014 Portable providers and channel boundaries\n\n### Privacy / security considerations\n\nNo behaviour change. The policy gate, confirmation manager, and audit logger stay in `ToolDispatcher` as the single choke-point before any `ToolEntry::execute` is called \u2014 the refactor does not move security logic, only implementation logic. The single call site (`ToolDispatcher::execute_with_context`) is preserved and is now easier to audit for issue #22.\n\n### Additional context\n\nelated issues:\n- #32 \u2014 `LlmBackend` abstraction (same pattern: trait-per-backend replaces match arms; this issue applies the same design to tools)\n- #22 \u2014 enforce tool-call gate (the single-choke-point requirement is preserved by this refactor)\n\nProposed new layout:\n\n```\ncrates/genie-core/src/tools/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 mod.rs          # re-exports ToolEntry, ToolDispatcher, ToolDispatcherConfig\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 registry.rs     # ToolRegistry\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 dispatcher.rs   # ToolDispatcher (middleware only)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 config.rs       # ToolDispatcherConfig\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 builtin/\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 home_control.rs\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 home_status.rs\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 home_undo.rs\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 action_history.rs\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 memory_recall.rs\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 memory_status.rs\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 memory_forget.rs\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 memory_store.rs\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 play_media.rs\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 set_timer.rs\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 get_time.rs\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 skill_runner.rs\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 get_weather.rs\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 web_search.rs\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 calculate.rs\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 system_info.rs\n```\n",
